<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-nī^gro</span></b> ,
		āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to blacken utterly, dye</i> or <i>color very black</i> (very rare; in the Ciceron.
			per. not at all). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram (amurca),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 55 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 6, 35, § 109</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capillum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					23, 5, 53, § 99</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">faciem super carbones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Thren. 4, 8</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: honorem famamque alicujus, <i>to blacken</i>, i. e. <i>to asperse,
				defame</i>, Firm. 5, 10 <i>fin.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
